# =============================================================
# ADS Thesis - Terminology drift in PTSD literature
# Reproducibility-rule: code + input data live in Git; light outputs do not.
# Running the scripts on a fresh clone should recreate every light output in
# outputs/ exactly as in the thesis. Heavy (GPU) outputs are committed.
# =============================================================

# ----- 1. Light-model outputs (ELAS u4 / TF-IDF) -------------
# Commit the FIGURES and aggregate SUMMARIES (the thesis figures + headline
# numbers) as evidence. The bulky, fully regenerable intermediates (per-run and
# per-cell results, the simulation-input CSVs) are ignored and rebuilt on CPU by
# code/SQ{1,2}/.
outputs/SQ1/simulations/runs/
outputs/SQ1/simulations/datasets/
outputs/SQ1/test.txt
outputs/SQ2/simulations/
outputs/SQ2/archive_per_occurrence_2026-06-02/

# ----- 1b. Heavy-model outputs (ELAS h3, committed) ----------
# Heavy results ARE committed as evidence: they need a GPU (Kaggle, see
# code/SQ{1,2}_heavy/KAGGLE_README.md) and cannot be regenerated on a fresh
# CPU clone. Only the large GPU embedding caches (~260 MB) are ignored - they
# are rebuilt on a GPU and are not needed for the downstream comparison.
outputs/SQ1_heavy/simulations/emb_cache/
outputs/SQ2_heavy/emb_cache/

# ----- 2. Regenerable intermediate data ----------------------
# Big parquet that build_regex_dataset.py recreates in ~30s
data/SQ2/foras_regex_rewritten.parquet

# ----- 3. Python noise ---------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ----- 4. Virtual envs ---------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ----- 5. OS / IDE noise -------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ----- 6. Local secrets / config -----------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem

# FORAS referenced_works cache (regenerable via --reverse-edges-only)
data/SQ1/foras_references_cache.jsonl
data/SQ1/raw/

# Deprecated pre-pivot candidate pool (the active pool is candidates_with_terms.csv)
data/SQ1/candidates_master.csv

# Build artefact (canonical copy lives in OneDrive Report/)
*.docx
